{"step_index":168,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-02T17:19:34Z","content":"The development of your **DevOps-Enabled Qualification Verification System (Java Spring Boot)** is complete.\n\nAll project files, automated CI/CD configurations, test suites, Docker orchestration, and academic deliverables have been created in:\n📁 **`C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system`**\n\nFor a detailed summary and guide, see the [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/brain/954a2aec-bd0d-40c2-b07d-d2f6e9c754b8/walkthrough.md).\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Overview of What Has Been Delivered\n\n#### 1. Core Software System (25 Marks + 10 Bonus Marks)\n* **Java 17 & Spring Boot 3 REST API**: Qualification lifecycle (issue, query, update, revoke) with Spring Data JPA.\n* **Cryptographic Tamper Resistance (Bonus Feature)**: Automated SHA-256 digital fingerprinting that flags altered or forged certificates.\n* **Public & Institutional Verification Portal**: Web UI with live verification badges (`GENUINE`, `REVOKED`, `ALTERED`, `NOT_FOUND`).\n* **Audit Trail Engine**: Immutable logging capturing verifier identity, timestamp, inquiring IP address, and outcome.\n* **Security & RBAC**: JWT authentication with `ROLE_ADMIN`, `ROLE_INSTITUTION`, and `ROLE_VERIFIER`.\n* **OpenAPI / Swagger**: Live interactive API testing available at `/swagger-ui.html`.\n\n#### 2. DevOps & CI/CD Implementation (20% Git Repo + 25% System)\n* **GitHub Actions Pipeline (`.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml`)**: 4-stage automated pipeline (Linting $\\rightarrow$ Testing & Coverage Gate $\\rightarrow$ JAR Packaging $\\rightarrow$ Docker Container Build).\n* **Quality Gates**: Maven Checkstyle for static analysis and JaCoCo enforcing $>80\\%$ line coverage.\n* **Containerization**: Multi-stage, minimal attack surface `Dockerfile` and `docker-compose.yml` with PostgreSQL.\n* **Git Collaboration**: GitFlow branching model guide, Pull Request templates, and Issue templates.\n\n#### 3. Academic Deliverables & Reports (25% Report + 15% Viva + 15% Contribution)\n* 📄 **[Technical Report Template (3,000–4,000 words)](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/docs/TECHNICAL_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md)**: Structured academic report covering problem analysis, requirements, architecture, ADRs, DevOps workflows, and evaluations.\n* 🎤 **[Viva Presentation & Demo Script](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/docs/VIVA_DEMO_SCRIPT.md)**: Timed 10–15 minute live presentation breakdown with visual demo steps.\n* 👥 **[Individual Contribution Guide](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/docs/INDIVIDUAL_CONTRIBUTION_GUIDE.md)**: Contribution evidence report template for team members.\n* 📘 **[Project README.md](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/README.md)**: System documentation, architecture diagrams, and quick-start guides.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 How to Run the Project\n\n1. **In IntelliJ IDEA / Eclipse / VS Code**:\n   * Open folder `C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system`.\n   * Run `QualificationVerificationApplication.java`.\n   * Open `http://localhost:8080` in your browser.\n2. **In Docker**:\n   ```bash\n   cd C:\\Users\\Madziva\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\qualification-verification-system\n   docker compose up --build\n   ```\n3. **To Push to GitHub and Trigger the CI/CD Pipeline**:\n   ```bash\n   git init\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"feat: initial commit of DevOps qualification verification system\"\n   git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo-name>.git\n   git branch -M main\n   git push -u origin main\n   ```\n\nLet me know if you would like to test or adjust any specific part of the system!"}
